      "writtenOn": "2015-05-14T00:14:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ok, sorry for the confusion here. what it basically does here is to:\n1. find the Issuer(client_issuer) from the client certificate referenced from env by \"CONF.tokenless_auth.issuer_attribute\"(SSL_CLIENT_I_DN)\n2. compare the Issuer(client_isser) if it matches with one of the trusted issuers defined in keystone.conf as the option \u0027trusted_issuer\u0027\n\nSSL_CLIENT_I_DN is always the attribute name in the env that references to the certificate\u0027s Issuer.\n\nFor example:\nenv \u003d { ...\n           \"SSL_CLIENT_I_DN\": \"CN\u003djohn,OU\u003dkeystone,O\u003dopenstack\"\n           ....\n          }\n\nkeystone.conf has the following defined:\ntrusted_isser\u003dCN\u003djohn,OU\u003dkeystone,O\u003dopenstack\ntrusted_isser\u003dCN\u003dmary,OU\u003deng,O\u003dabc\n\nthe client_issuer is trusted as it matches with an entry in keystone.conf.\n\nhope this clears the confusion.",
      "parentUuid": "9a0c5dc1_eff9c34e",
      "revId": "7ef63b95713a9ba82ca47ac1670a17bfe034efbf",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
